EXT. STAGECOACH STATION - HIGH NOON

A single hitching post. Dust. A water trough with a drowned sparrow in it.

SHERIFF LUCINDA HARGROVE (40s, star on her vest) stands with her arms folded. Beside her, DEPUTY MARIGOLD TEASDALE (20s, new hat, too-big holster) fidgets. Across the road, a rider on a grey mare: ABSALOM FINCH (30s, handlebar moustache, silver spurs).

LUCINDA
(to Marigold, low)
Let me do the talking.

MARIGOLD
I wasn't going to.

LUCINDA
(to the road, loud)
Morning, Absalom.

ABSALOM
Morning, Sheriff.

LUCINDA
You're a long way from Tucson.

ABSALOM
It's a long way to anywhere.

He swings down. Spurs ring. The mare shakes her mane. Marigold's hand drifts toward her holster.

LUCINDA
(muttering)
Hand off the gun.

MARIGOLD
(muttering)
She said hand off.

She lets the hand fall. Lucinda doesn't look at her.

ABSALOM
Heard there was a hanging today.

LUCINDA
Heard wrong.

ABSALOM
Heard right, then.

He tips his hat to the trough, to the sparrow, to the dust. Mounts again, turns the mare, and trots out of town. Lucinda watches him go. Marigold releases her breath.

MARIGOLD
Who hangs on a Tuesday?

LUCINDA
(to the whole street)
Nobody, thank God.

FADE OUT.
